mutant-tvalid_waits_for_tready-w64: the defect the mux's own comment records: TVALID made to wait for TREADY
mutant-tdata_hidden_while_stalled-w8: the output TDATA is gated by TREADY, so it moves while stalled
mutant-tkeep_hidden_while_stalled-w64: the output TKEEP is gated by TREADY, so it moves while stalled
mutant-tlast_hidden_while_stalled-w8: the output TLAST is gated by TREADY, so it rises only at the handshake
mutant-released_while_tlast_stalled-w64: s0 gives up the output on a TLAST beat the sink has not taken
mutant-released_before_tlast_s0-w8: s0 gives up the output after any beat, not after its TLAST beat
mutant-released_before_tlast_s1-w64: s1 gives up the output after any beat, not after its TLAST beat
mutant-kept_after_tlast-w8: s1 keeps the output after its TLAST beat
mutant-reset_ignored-w64: the state register ignores reset, so an owner survives it
mutant-illegal_state_reached-w64: a grant decodes to the encoding no state name owns
mutant-granted_without_request-w8: the arbiter grants s1 whether or not it offers a beat
mutant-both_sources_ready-w64: s1 also sees TREADY while s0 owns the output
mutant-ready_ignores_sink-w8: s0 sees TREADY while the sink is stalling the output
mutant-tkeep_from_other_source-w64: an s1 beat leaves with s0's TKEEP
scoreboard-round_robin_inverted-w8: the arbiter prefers the source it just served; no property claims fairness, so the scoreboard must catch it
elaboration-tdata_width_12: gen_guard_tdata_width must refuse a TDATA width that is not whole bytes
coverage-assertions_disabled-w64: --no-assert compiles every assertion, and every witness with it, out of a bound checker
